<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">events</ansi>

Now and then the road stops your company: a rope over a gorge, a
stranger at a fire, a burned shrine. A scene opens as a page of text
with numbered choices. Answer it, and what you chose happens.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">When a scene opens</ansi>

  - You walk into a place that has one (a ruin, a lair's door, a spot on
    the road), or a journey ends in a zone that does.
  - You finish a camp rest, and the camp has a visitor.
  - Each scene comes once for your company, or again after a long wait if
    it is the kind that returns. It is remembered through a restart.
  - Never in a fight, on a journey, or while you rest.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Answering</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">choose 2</ansi>    take the second choice
  <ansi fg="command">event</ansi>       read the waiting page again

Your company stays where it is until you answer, and a page you leave
waiting is still there after you log out. Every page has a way out.
In the web client the page opens on its own screen: click a choice or
press its number key. Close the screen and type <ansi fg="command">event</ansi> to bring it back.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Who does it</ansi>

A choice may need a skill, a class, a temperament, a good or evil heart
or a certain level. The best member present who qualifies takes it, and
the page names them: <ansi fg="black-bold">(Sera, chancy)</ansi>. A choice nobody qualifies for shows
as <ansi fg="black-bold">(closed: needs a rogue)</ansi>; recruit differently and it opens. A choice
that asks for nothing is yours, as the leader.

Some choices are risky. The page says so in words: a small risk, chancy,
a long shot. The better the member does it (their skill, or their level),
the safer it is.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What can happen</ansi>

  - Wounds and ailments, for the one who took the risk or for everyone.
  - Hunger, thirst or tiredness.
  - Supplies, items and gold gained or lost.
  - Companions thinking better or worse of you (<ansi fg="command">help alignment</ansi>).
  - A fight with a named group.
  - Being carried to another place, or a mark the company keeps, which
    can change what later scenes offer.

Nothing here moves the world's clock, and the gains are small: a scene is
a choice with a cost, not a place to farm.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help travel</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help ailments</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>.
